---
title: "setLegionAddress / getLegionAddress (LegionAddressRegistry)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_op: determine operation type
    q_check_op --> q_set_check_auth: setLegionAddress called
    q_check_op --> q_get_lookup: getLegionAddress called
    q_set_check_auth --> q_revert_auth: caller not owner
    q_revert_auth --> [*]: revert Unauthorized
    q_set_check_auth --> q_set_validate: caller is owner
    q_set_validate --> q_set_store: address != address(0)
    q_set_validate --> q_revert_zero: zero address
    q_revert_zero --> [*]: revert InvalidAddress
    q_set_store --> [*]: registry[key] = address, emit AddressUpdated
    q_get_lookup --> [*]: return registry[key]

    note right of q_set_store
        INV-001: only owner can update registry entries
        INV-002: registry is the single source of truth for Legion infrastructure addresses
        INV-003: contracts call syncLegionAddresses to pull updated values
    end note
